{
    "background_story": "Clayton was a charismatic salesman with a gift for gab. His garrulity was both a blessing and a curse. On the one hand, his ability to talk effortlessly about anything and everything made him a natural people person, able to connect with clients and close deals with ease. However, his tendency to dominate conversations often left others struggling to get a word in edgewise. Clayton's colleagues would often joke that he could talk the ears off a cornfield, and his family would lovingly roll their eyes at his lengthy stories. Despite this, Clayton's garrulity also made him a beloved fixture in the community, always ready with a joke, a anecdote, or a sympathetic ear. His verbosity may have been a challenge for some, but it was also a key part of his charm.",
